  "conclusions_and_hypotheses": {
    "verified_observations": [
      "Baseline reproduction is 100% verified against frozen model (SHA256: 41e61760fc...) and test dataset (SHA256: 7f9d0ce56b...), yielding 621 trades, \u20b952,528.87 gross P&L, \u20b9213,207.51 friction, and -\u20b9160,678.64 net P&L.",
      "The model generates weak class probability separation: mean P(BUY) for true BUYs is 0.3069 vs 0.2904 for non-BUYs (separation of only 1.65 percentage points).",
      "Friction was catastrophic to strategy viability: statutory delivery friction and slippage totaled \u20b9213,207.51 (405.89% of gross net alpha and 21.32% of initial portfolio capital).",
      "Low-conviction trades caused 100% of the portfolio's net loss: trades entered in P(BUY) in [0.33, 0.40) lost -\u20b9106,335.06 in gross alpha and burned \u20b9120,966.94 in friction, generating -\u20b9227,302.00 net P&L across 350 trades (56.4% of all trades).",
      "High-conviction trades P(BUY) >= 0.40 were profitable after full friction: 271 trades generated +\u20b9158,863.93 gross P&L, \u20b992,240.57 friction, and +\u20b966,623.36 net P&L.",
      "Exit mechanisms exhibited severe asymmetric performance: early exits triggered by model SELL signals were profitable (+\u20b9160,893.61 net across 337 trades), while 5-day time-stop exits were catastrophic (-\u20b9307,827.78 net across 276 trades).",
      "Portfolio capacity constraints blocked 1,383 candidate BUY signals due to the 10-position ceiling while positions were held to day 5."
    ],
    "plausible_explanations_requiring_testing": [
